   "html_text": "Self-knowledge is especially secure, epistemically. Self-knowledge is (sometimes) acquired by use of an exclusively first-personal method. Our capacity for self-knowledge reflects our cognitive agency. One’s pronouncements about one’s own mental states carry a special authority or presumption of truth.",
